# ---- ADDENDUM 2026-11-06 · 3.132 Voicing (7th, 9th, rootless 9) and the jazz progressions (everything above kept verbatim — Axiom 9)
# his words: "i also want to be able to make lofi" (2026-11-05) · "yes" (2026-11-06, to the Lofi setup: specs/eravos.lofi-setup.spec)
voicing:
  - new choice Voicing [tension, 7th, 9th, rootless 9] def tension — "tension" is today's rule (triad → add9 → 7sus4 → cluster by TENSION),
    exactly, so nothing that exists changes; the others stack the scale's own thirds on the degree: 7th = 1 3 5 7 · 9th = 1 3 5 7 9 ·
    rootless 9 = 3 5 7 9 (the jazz piano's left hand — the Bassline plays the root)
  - TENSION shapes only the "tension" voicing; with 7th, 9th or rootless 9 it does nothing, so it dims and says why (DESIGN-GUIDE W7)
progressions: the five, then the jazz six (MusicParts.ALL_PROGRESSIONS); default unchanged (i-VI-III-VII)
proof: chord-gen tests — the default voicing equals the old rule for every degree and tension; 7th / 9th / rootless 9 are the scale's thirds

